{
 "id": "yinsh",
 "name": "Yinsh",
 "description": "Kris Burm's game of rings and markers on an 85-point board: drop a marker in a ring and move the ring, turning over the markers it jumps. Make rows of five to remove your rings; remove three to win.",
 "version": "0.1.0",
 "designers": ["Kris Burm"],
 "engine": "ruleset",
 "rules": [
  "Yinsh is played on a board of 85 points joined by lines in three directions. Each player has 5 rings (white and black); the two share a pool of 51 markers, white on one side and black on the other.",
  "Setup: starting with White, the players take turns placing a ring each on any empty point, until all 10 rings are on the board. Then White makes the first move.",
  "A turn: choose one of your rings and drop a marker of your colour inside it (the point it stands on). Then move that ring in a straight line along the lines, to any empty point: it may pass over empty points and over groups of markers, but it cannot pass over or land on another ring. If it jumps a group of markers, it must land on the first empty point after them, and every marker it jumped is turned over to the other colour.",
  "A row of five markers of one colour in a line is removed by its owner: when you have such a row after your move, take the five markers and also one of your own rings off the board (that ring is your score). A row of more than five lets you pick any five in a row; several rows are removed one after the other, so overlapping rows may break each other. If a move makes rows for both players, you remove yours first, then your opponent removes theirs.",
  "The first player to remove three rings wins. In the one-ring 'blitz' variant the first ring wins. If the last marker is placed on the board, the game ends and the player who removed more rings wins (equal is a draw).",
  "Interpretations: removed markers go back to the pool; a player who cannot move any ring passes. The game is decided on rings removed after 1000 plies."
 ],
 "params": {
  "rings": 5,
  "rings_to_win": 3,
  "markers": 51,
  "max_plies": 1000
 },
 "guide": { "tabs": [ { "id": "rules", "title": "Rules", "file": "rules.md" } ] },
